step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a simple mean of all 19 models to see baseline performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the full pool to see if inverse-error weighting improves over the simple mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the full pool to see if it outperforms the inverse-error weighted mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a trimmed‐mean on the full pool to see if trimming the outliers improves the already strong median result.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a best_single strategy using the top model ONLY_CWT_rf to see if a single strong model beats the trimmed mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ONLY_CWT_rf"}

Thought: Test a DBA combination on a selective pool to see if it improves over best_single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a weighted inverse‑error combination on the selective pool1 to see if weighting improves over the unweighted mean/median on that pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median on pool2 to see if a different selective pool improves over best_single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Test a simple mean on the selective pool1 to see if averaging fewer models can beat best_single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a trimmed‑mean on the selective pool1 to see if trimming improves over the mean and weighted pool1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool1","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the full pool using inverse_error weighting to see if it outperforms the best single model.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple mean on pool2 to see if averaging the slightly larger selective set improves over best_single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the more selective pool2 using inverse_error to see if a different weighting on a smaller set improves over best_single.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

